ood cuz like I finally did  something like no it's like  really noticeable and like it was good  Athena earned a full ride to Harvard  University I'm actually here it's it's  pretty it's really surreal in a way she  just finished her first year and is  studying to become a neuroscientist the  battle number truly feels over do you  feel as though you had to make it yeah  like I didn't feel like there was an  option of like failing because because I  had my mom was depending on it you sound  like you were trying to be the rock for  your mom I we were kind of each other's  rock I'd say yeah because it was kind of  like hard on both of us and so I wanted  to like make sure that she was so  smiling she is smiling and while they  continue to live in the shelter they're  looking ahead  so I came from somewhere that's a bit  more difficult I'm not leaving it behind  us and forgetting about it but taking  that as a learning experience showing  that in every one of us there's more  than meets the eye  Oh II know I can't say enough about her  she is just moving and shaking in her  new setting she loves the whole notion  of learning she wants to go back to  summer school and then next year is like  it just does not stop and and the police  her police work really is near and dear  to her heart she is such a trooper in  her precinct and and the other officers  there so appreciate her and just are  astounded by what she's been able to do  that they're still in the shelter I mean  it's an that is reality yeah yeah and  thank God they have a place where they  can be that safe like that which doesn't  happen it's lovely to see what she and  her mom have done for each other  Michelle what an amazing story yeah
 

